findings.claim:
Route 5 sends Lemmas 2.1.12–2.1.13 to SmoothRepresentationsOfLocalGroups:SR.1 as a source. These lemmas are Bushnell–Kutzko's cover formalism:
- the algebra map t : H(Δ_M,U_M) → H(Δ,U) [BK98, Cor. 6.12];
- strongly positive elements;
- the extension of t to an isomorphism after inverting [UzU].
SR.1's text plans convolution algebras, normalized idempotents and the e_U-corner equivalence. It plans no monoid Hecke algebras, covers or strongly positive elements. The same formalism is already owned by the pending SmoothRepresentationsPartII ('types, depth and the construction of supercuspidal representations'):
- PAPER-STEVENS-08/283, '[BK2, Theorem 7.2] and the notions it uses: decomposed pairs, strongly positive elements, G-covers', is routed there;
- so is PAPER-LUST-STEVENS-20's Bushnell–Kutzko cover diagram;
- PAPER-FINTZEN-21's brief for it builds 'G-covers'.
The lemmas therefore have two owners.

The owner of Theorems 2.4.10 and 2.4.11 is unsettled. Item 83 (Theorem 2.4.10(1)) is marked planned at AS.5 and ALS.5. Its proof rests on two cited results that no stage plans and no item states: [BW00, Ch. II, Prop. 3.1] and [Clo90, Lem. 3.14] with the Künneth formula. The item's own note concedes this. Route 4 sends Theorem 2.4.10(2) and Theorem 2.4.11 (items 84, 85 and 87) to ArithmeticLocallySymmetricSpaces, whose summary confines it to 'topological cohomology and boundary geometry'. Their proofs also need the Galois representations of Theorems 2.3.2 and 2.3.3 (AG2.4, AG2.2) to kill the Eisenstein summands. ALS.5 imports none of these, and route 4's reason does not say that it must. Two accepted extractions disagree with this extraction:
- PAPER-BOXER-CALEGARI-GEE-ETAL-25/40 marks ACC+ Theorem 2.4.10 planned at AS.5 and AG2.0;
- PAPER-SCHOLZE-15/127 marks the Clozel input missing, in a source route of ALS.5.

